---
import SaidDocsLayout from "../../../layouts/SaidDocsLayout.astro";
import SaidShot from "../../../components/SaidShot.astro";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  name: "Set up Said and Done.: first boot to first page",
  description:
    "Install Said and Done., point it at your notes folder, and land on a working record.",
  step: [
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Install Said and Done." },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Point it at your notes folder" },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Decide on the expedition" },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Make the first page" },
  ],
};
---

<SaidDocsLayout
  title="First boot, first page — Said and Done. guides"
  description="Install Said and Done., point it at your notes folder, and land on a working record — in about two minutes."
  section="guides"
  kicker="Guide 01"
  heading="First boot, first page"
  dek="About two minutes, one folder decision."
  slug="first-boot"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p>
    Said and Done. arrives whole: the installer carries everything it needs, and
    nothing is downloaded at boot. Your only real decision is which folder holds
    your notes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="install">1 · Install</h2>
  <p>
    Run the installer for your platform. On Linux it installs to your own user
    and adds the launcher entry. On macOS you drag Said and Done. to
    Applications. On Windows it installs per-user with a normal uninstaller. No
    elevation, no system folders — and uninstalling never touches your data.
  </p>

  <h2 id="notes">2 · Point it at your notes</h2>
  <p>
    First boot asks one thing first: where do your notes live? Walk to the
    folder that holds your work and take it. Every folder inside becomes a
    notebook; nothing is copied or moved. No notes folder yet? Take the
    suggested fresh one and grow into it.
  </p>
  <SaidShot
    src="/said-and-done/shots/wizard-folder.png"
    alt="The first-boot folder picker, walking the home folder"
    caption="First boot walks your own folders — nothing is made until you choose."
  />

  <h2 id="expedition">3 · Want the expedition?</h2>
  <p>
    One last thing: <strong>Mars or Bust</strong> — a worked example of the desk.
    Two survivors, a dog, two hundred files of surviving and shipbuilding, and the
    fifty pages it takes to fly. Take it aboard and it becomes your selected notebook,
    free and never counted against the plan — or start with an empty desk.
  </p>

  <h2 id="first-page">4 · The first page</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Press <code>n</code> — a new page opens.</li>
    <li>Give it a title in your own words.</li>
    <li>
      Press <code>enter</code> — it lands on the record, numbered for life.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    That's the whole loop. Say it, work it, and when it's finished — mark it
    done. <strong>Said and Done.</strong>
  </p>
</SaidDocsLayout>
